    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** stands out as our clear-cut priority play with an elite score of 71.46. While he faces Fried, the park factors in his favor, coupled with a significant boost from an \"out\" wind and an optimal leadoff spot, make him the anchor of our lineup. **Cal Raleigh** (66.77) and **Bryson Stott** (63.77) follow closely; **Raleigh** benefits from a porous 4.76 xERA matchup against McCullers Jr., while **Stott** receives a critical boost from the favorable wind and a platoon-advantage matchup against Gray. These three should provide the heavy lifting for our HR and RBI totals as we attempt to mitigate the sting of facing elite arms like Ohtani and Jax.\n\nOur toughest roster management decision involved leaving **Matt Chapman** (43.58) on the bench. Despite a decent base projection, his lower slot in the batting order against the formidable Ohtani suppressed his efficiency score below our threshold, ultimately costing him a spot behind the higher-upside profiles of **Masyn Winn** and **Daulton Varsho**. We are playing the margins heavily today, specifically banking on the speed and stolen base potential of **Winn**\u2014who benefits from a slow-delivering pitcher\u2014to help us gain ground in our scarcest category. Be advised that while **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Jonathan Aranda** are set to start, both face moderate-to-tough SPs; monitor the late-afternoon weather reports, as the wind-out conditions at **Ward**\u2019s and **Stott**\u2019s venues could turn marginal fly balls into crucial extra-base hits.",
